## Aim
To calculate the frequency distribution of ages of customers who made purchases in the past month using Pandas.

## Algorithm
1. Start the program and import Pandas.
2. Create a DataFrame containing customer IDs, ages and order dates.
3. Convert order dates into datetime format.
4. Select customers who made purchases in the past month.
5. Calculate the frequency of customer ages using `value_counts()`.
6. Display the frequency distribution.

## Input

| Customer ID | Age | Order Date |
|---|---:|---|
| 101 | 20 | 2026-10-20 |
| 102 | 25 | 2026-10-25 |
| 103 | 30 | 2026-11-01 |
| 104 | 20 | 2026-11-05 |
| 105 | 25 | 2026-11-10 |
| 106 | 35 | 2026-11-15 |

## Output

```text
Frequency Distribution of Customer Ages:
Age
20    2
25    2
30    1
35    1
```

## Code

```python
import pandas as pd

data = {
    "Customer_ID": [101, 102, 103, 104, 105, 106],
    "Age": [20, 25, 30, 20, 25, 35],
    "Order_Date": ["2026-10-20", "2026-10-25",
                   "2026-11-01", "2026-11-05",
                   "2026-11-10", "2026-11-15"]
}

df = pd.DataFrame(data)

df["Order_Date"] = pd.to_datetime(df["Order_Date"])

one_month_ago = pd.Timestamp.today() - pd.DateOffset(months=1)

recent = df[df["Order_Date"] >= one_month_ago]

frequency = recent["Age"].value_counts().sort_index()

print("Frequency Distribution of Customer Ages:")
print(frequency)
```

## Result
The frequency distribution of customer ages who made purchases in the past month was calculated successfully using Pandas.

